 want  to go with each variant that is reviewed  or curated  so again you know just depends on the  content of the panel  that you are sequencing and reporting  and again you know  if you're identifying you know variants  of unknown significance tier three  variants or  any any other variant that might require  that additional  uh review it's really at the discretion  of the end user but for us you know if  we have a negative report it takes it's  very quick to generate that you know  from the time we upload the vcf about 30  seconds to the report  if we're identifying well-known variants  you know maybe a minute or two  five to ten minutes at the longest  all right thank you  next question  how long is a typical uncle mine  reporter report  again yes so another great question yeah  and again this uh also depends  um the report is completely modifiable  so  any section that we choose to include on  the report or exclude can either reduce  or add to the length of that report  for us you know a negative report would  be about a page or two  for  one with a variant that say has  assigned clinical trials or therapies  those can extend a little longer you  know anywhere from  3 to 11 pages and those are just for the  reports that we're generating  if you add additional sections in there  i think one of the sections that we  don't include on our report are gene  descriptions  on that report you know there's things  that will add to the length so if you're  looking for  a lengthier report you're able to make  that if you're looking for a short  compact report that can go out  you're able to achieve that as well but  overall um the reports that we're  generating out of our laboratory are are  relatively i would say relatively  compact  thank you  next question how often does uncle mind  reporter update content  um so for us at least what we're seeing  currently is that we're getting updates  on a monthly basis uh we're seeing those  come through for the  standalone and the integrated versions  of the  software  if configured within the  genexis system those updates can be  as simple as an automatic i don't say  automatic but you know clicking an icon  within the  software to update that content  when they do update the content they  provide all of the  updates and changes that uh have been  made there whether it's anything with  the  variant classification any additional um  guideline recommendations or therapies  trials  update to genes available  uh gene descriptions etc so it's a  pretty comprehensive  um  update packet  that is provided depending on the extent  of the update  but all that information is available  there it's typically on a monthly basis  right  thank you  next question is  can we use customized panels from third  parties or does it have to be through  thermo fisher  so from from my understanding for the  usage of oncoming reporter the vcf file  that is generated needs to come through  either the ion reporter platform or the  genexis platform  so whatever data that is being generated  in order to push that through oncoming  reporter  would have to be analyzed in either of  those platforms  thank you  next question  can someone with a basic knowledge of  bioinformatics  utilize this platform for data analysis  with ease  i would say so um you know i i think you  know within our laboratory  we have a  trained bioinformatician but for the  rest of us you know none of us have that  classical bioinformatics background  and  we found that as a team that we're  readily able to navigate these platforms  and software's  without needing to have that necessarily  in-depth background um  uh education but um it's it's a fairly  straightforward platform to to utilize  you  next question  can  um how does the uncle mine reporter get  access to what is to be analyzed  uh so for  for our needs within our laboratory  we're downloading uh  if we're talking about the standalone  version  we're downloading a filtered vcf file  from the genexis software from our data  analysis so that vcf file that's  generated  within the platform is then uploaded  into the software  if we're talking about the integrated  version it's utilizing the data that's  currently within the platform so when we  want to move forward or advance with a  report using that integrated mode  all the data that's needed  is pulled directly from the gen x's  platform so  sandalin  for us we're downloading a file and  uploading in the integrated mode it's  simply having that  making that choice or election to uh  install the oncoming reporter  software there and then once that's  enabled  navigating through the the software to  have that data  uh report generated  thank you and we will wrap up with that  question  do you have any final comments for our  audience  i know just thank you for for attending  today thank you for your time i really  appreciate it and hope i was able to  provide you with some  good information or details about a  pokemon  well reporter you again dr seidman for  your time today and your important  research  we would also like to thank lab roots  and our sponsor thermo fisher scientific  for underwriting today's educational  webcast  before we go i'd like to thank the  audience for joining us today and for  their interesting questions  questions we did not have time for today  and those submitted during the on-demand  period will be addressed by the speaker  via the contact information you provided  at the time of registration  this webcast can be viewed on demand lab  routes will alert you via email when  it's available for replay we encourage  you to share that email with your  colleagues who may have missed today's  live event  until next time goodbye  you

